# mi nitcu lo da'i [cu'i] lojbo valcku

Given an ontology whereby {da da'i broda} is true for any value of
broda, your solution is close to the solution that the Jboske discussion
settled on (i.e. Kinds), but with certain key differences:

"mi nitcu lo da'i [cu'i] lojbo valcku"
"There is a (real or imaginary) jbodictionary I need"

is not falsified by

"mi nitcu lo da'i [cu'i] lojbo valcku na ku"
"There is a (real or imaginary) jbodictionary I don't need"

whereas "I need a book" (on the so-called ANY/'opaque' reading)
IS falsified by "There is a (real or imaginary) book that I don't need".

--And.





